<x-layout title="Privacy at Folkscript"><div class="legal-page"><h1>A little privacy.<br>A lot of respect.</h1><div class="prose"><p>This notice describes the data handled by this Folkscript installation. Before a public launch, the operator must add their legal identity, contact details, applicable retention periods, and any region-specific rights or service disclosures.</p><h2>What your account contains</h2><p>We store your name, email address, securely hashed password, and the profile details you choose to provide. Your public name, username, biography, and published stories are visible to readers. Your email address and private drafts are not public.</p><h2>Reading and participating</h2><p>Bookmarks, follows, reactions, and comments are stored to provide those features. Session cookies keep you signed in and protect forms from misuse. A browser preference remembers your color theme. Story views are counted without third-party advertising trackers in the default configuration.</p><h2>Optional services</h2><p>If the operator configures payment or social login providers, those services process data according to their own policies. Folkscript does not store card numbers. Email delivery and storage providers may process account messages and media when enabled.</p><h2>Your controls</h2><p>You can edit your profile, choose whether to receive digests, revoke API access tokens, and delete your account from Settings. The operator should provide a verified contact route for access, export, and deletion requests before opening registration publicly.</p></div></div></x-layout>
